  "_meta": {
    "description": "Vietnamese industrial/workplace TERMS (not whole phrases) with en/zh/ko equivalents.",
    "rationale": "NLLB-200-distilled-600M loses Vietnamese domain compounds: 'xe nang' becomes 'the train', 'may nen khi' becomes 'the air'. Substituting the English term into the Vietnamese source before translation recovers them in every target language (measured 2026-08-19). This file is the substitution table; industrial_phrases.json remains the whole-utterance memory.",
    "scope": "Terms only. Keep entries short and unambiguous - a long entry is a phrase and belongs in industrial_phrases.json. Expanded 2026-08-20 after the T4 run measured term recovery at 0.441 on translated sentences: coverage, not the mechanism, is the limit.",
    "source": "Authored for this project. Not verified by a native zh/ko reviewer; see the caveat in glossary_mt.py."
